{"term":"swallow","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:aa51c605b66ffc5a07","definition":"To cause (food, drink etc.) to pass from the mouth into the stomach; to take into the stomach through the throat.","example":"What the liquor was I do not know, but it was not so strong but that I could swallow it in great gulps and found it less burning than my burning throat.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["consume","devour","eat","gulp"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2497b19b63ccb04db0","definition":"To take (something) in so that it disappears; to consume, absorb.","example":"The necessary provision of the life swallows the greatest part of their time.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["absorb","engulf","incorporate","swallow up","absorb","add on","assimilate","co-opt","corporate","incorporate","incorpse","integrate","subsume","swallow"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ff4e1f46c714e08536","definition":"To take food down into the stomach; to make the muscular contractions of the oesophagus to achieve this, often taken as a sign of nervousness or strong emotion.","example":"My throat was so sore that I was unable to swallow.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["gulp"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1f036021b27e3229a7","definition":"To accept easily or without questions; to believe, accept.","example":"this humbug was readily swallowed by men who were supposed to be intelligent,","pos":"verb","synonyms":["buy","credit"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:857308b9b8dabc9d90","definition":"To engross; to appropriate; usually with up.","example":"Homer excels […] in this, that he swallowed up the honour of those who succeeded him.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["absorb","monopolize","occupy","take over"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:35eacce5972ad2eac6","definition":"To retract; to recant.","example":"to swallow one's opinions","pos":"verb","synonyms":["disavow","take back","abjure","backpedal","disavow","disown","eat one's words","recall","recant","retract","revoke","swallow","take back","unsay","unspeak","walk back","withcall","withdraw"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5e56056b7a5660784f","definition":"To put up with; to bear patiently or without retaliation.","example":"to swallow an affront or insult","pos":"verb","synonyms":["endure","live with","abear","abide","aby","accept","allow","bear","bide","brook","dree","endure","forbear","go along with","live with","pass","pocket","pouch","put up with","stand","stick","stomach","suffer","swallow","take","take sitting down","thole","tolerate","undergang","undergo"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d51b07c3abc32e3ce1","definition":"To swallow semen after oral sex, as opposed to spitting it out.","example":"Was she straight or was she gay? Did she spit or swallow? Was she smooth or hairy down there? Questions, questions.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"euphemistic, slang, vulgar","register":"euphemistic, slang, vulgar","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:37e6b8dabe0004b6b4","definition":"The amount swallowed in one gulp; the act of swallowing.","example":"He took the aspirin with a single swallow of water.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["midswallow","swallow hole"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d995457b9681f1d5b3","definition":"A deep chasm or abyss in the earth.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["midswallow","swallow hole"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:23254ab2ac228c428d","definition":"The mouth and throat; that which is used for swallowing; the gullet.","example":"The door burst wide open, and he saw nothing but a gaping jaw extending from the threshold up to the lintel. \"There is a mouthful for you,\" said the youngster, and threw the pauper boy into the swallow; \"taste that! But let me see now who you are! Perhaps you are an old acquaintance?\" And so it was; it was the devil who was about again.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["midswallow","swallow hole"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cb3bb8deed9ab4d339","definition":"The opening in a pulley block between the sheave and shell through which the rope passes.","example":"In addition, j-lock shackles can pass through the swallow of a modern genoa track even with a sheet in tension already there, and this is very useful when preparing a sail change on the same tack.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["midswallow","swallow hole"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0f382e14f7f3637ad1","definition":"Any of various carbohydrate-based dishes that are swallowed without much chewing, commonly paired and eaten with various types of soup.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Nigeria","register":"Nigeria, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["midswallow","swallow hole"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:612ad6930c1e70af42","definition":"A small, migratory bird of the Hirundinidae family with long, pointed, moon-shaped wings and a forked tail which feeds on the wing by catching insects.","exa